B.ckQ=new A.eN("15","WEEK 15 \u2014 Fetal age 13 weeks \u2014 3.5 months",2,"~16.7 cm (6.6 inches), ~117 grams",B.bwp,B.e9)
B.bky=s(["The average 16-week fetus is 7.3 inches (18.6 cm) long and weighs 5.2 ounces (146 grams).","Hearing is beginning to form.","The pancreas begins to produce exocrine enzymes.","The canalicular period of lung development has started and will continue until about 25 weeks.","The average 17-week fetus is 8 inches (20.4 cm) long and weighs 6.4 ounces (181 grams).","The pseudoglandular stage of lung development ends at about 17 weeks. There are still no alveoli (the air sacs in the lungs where the exchange of oxygen and carbon dioxide occurs), so respiration is not possible at this time."],t.s)
